{
  "comment": [
    "UNION ALL phase 4: a compound in a value position — IN, NOT IN and scalar.",
    "",
    "Nine classes and one that cannot be written. They attack the arity contract",
    "phase four introduced: the two rules, which are two and not one, and where the",
    "number each is checked against comes from. Three of them attack rules older",
    "than this phase — nested parenthesisation, global numbering, the phase two",
    "comparison — because a value position is another public route to each, and a",
    "route with no test is a route the rule is not proven on.",
    "",
    "Kept apart from the other four manifests, whose accounting is closed. UNION ALL",
    "is not frozen and this is not the UNION manifest.",
    "",
    "Every killer runs in the root module and needs no database. What a server has",
    "to settle — SQL type compatibility, and how many rows a scalar subquery may",
    "return — is in internal/gendemo/m16_unionvalue_test.go, which is not part of",
    "this campaign."
  ],
  "evidence_commit": "ab3e1df",
  "evidence_commit_note": [
    "ab3e1df is the revision every UNION ALL class was last applied to and run at, in a",
    "worktree checked out at exactly that commit, with the manifests read and written",
    "outside it so the tree stayed clean between classes. It is kept reachable as",
    "archive/m16-union-mutation-evidence.",
    "",
    "The five UNION ALL campaigns were rerun together at one revision after `mutate",
    "anchors` found four anchors that later phases had silently invalidated by editing",
    "the code they quote. An anchor that no longer matches makes its class look like a",
    "survivor, so the campaigns were pinned to revisions where they no longer ran.",
    "They run again, and three harness controls were active: anchors still quote their",
    "code, every site names the function its anchor is inside, and each semantic probe",
    "survives every mutation in another function."
  ],
  "not_expressible": [
    {
      "id": "P4-9",
      "name": "A foreign implementation of the value-subquery capability is accepted",
      "why": [
        "ValueTerm is closed by an unexported method, so a type outside the package",
        "cannot satisfy it and no code runs to decide whether it does. There is",
        "nothing to mutate: the rule is the Go compiler's.",
        "",
        "It is asserted instead by four compile-fail cases, each of which compiles a",
        "whole program and requires it to fail: a foreign type in a scalar position,",
        "a foreign type in a membership test, a write in a scalar position, and a",
        "value known only as a SourceTerm in a scalar position. The last of those is",
        "the one that proves the two read capabilities did not collapse into one."
      ]
    }
  ],
